\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Make me a captive, Lord,
\par And then I shall be free;
\par Force me to render up my sword,
\par And I shall conqueror be.
\par I sit in life's alarm
\par When by myself I stand;
\par Imprison me within Thine arms,
\par And strong shall be my hand.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. My heart is weak and poor
\par Untill it master find;
\par It has no spring of action sure-
\par It varies with the wind.
\par It cannot freely move,
\par Till Thou hast wrought its chain;
\par Enslave it with Thy matchless love,
\par And deathless it shall reign.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My power is faint and low
\par Till I have learned to serve;
\par It wants the needed fire to glow,
\par It wants the breeze to nerve;
\par It cannot drive the world,
\par Until itself be driven;
\par Its flag can only be unfurled
\par When Thou shalt breathe from heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My will is not my own
\par Till Thou hast made it Thine;
\par If it would reach a monarch's throne
\par It must its crown resign;
\par It only stands umbent,
\par Amid the clashing strife,
\par When on Thy bosom it has leant
\par And found in Thee its life.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

